    "created_at": "2016-06-25T05:01:09Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-06-25T05:01:09Z",
    "body": "Providing a flat view of the descriptors is definitely an improvement over manually requesting the and re-parsing the configuration descriptor. However, in many cases, the user would still end up responsible for building up enough of the tree structure to distinguish between a relevant class descriptor associated with interface 2, alt setting 0 vs an unrelated class descriptor associated interface 1, alt setting 1.\n\nWould it make sense for each descriptor in the normal tree view to have an attribute storing the corresponding index in the linear view? That would make it possible for the user code to use the existing tree structure to skip straight to the interface/endpoint of interest and parse only a small subset of the linear view.\n\nThis would be similar to the way that handle ranges in the BLE GATT protocol are used to associate a service with all of its characteristics and descriptors.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
